      "text": "VT-2\nDOERBIRDS\n\u201cEXACUE BELLATORES AERIOS\u201d\nCDR J. L. HATHAWAY NAS WHITING FIELD, FL CDR L. S. SCHAFF\nCommanding Officer Executive Officer\nSunday, 15-Nov-2026\nSUNRISE: 0615 MOONRISE: 1129 % ILLUM: 29%\nSUNSET: 1651 MOONSET: 2207 JULIAN DATE: 6319\nTOTAL ADV: 16 TOTAL FLY EVENTS: 16/16 TOTAL FLY HRS: 25.6 TOTAL SIM EVENTS: 0 TOTAL SIM HRS: 0.0\nQuestions:\nEP Question: GENERATOR FAILURE\nNATOPS: Electrical System\nSOP: (T-6B) ___________ AND/OR ____________ LIGHTS SHALL NOT BE SECURED PRIOR TO THE PROPELLER ROTATION STOPPING.\nDUTY/WATCH ASSIGNED SIGN IN SIGN OUT\nSDO TOLLISON, BENJAMIN# 0800 0800\nSUPER RUSH, WILLIAM# 0800 0759\nWEEKEND CDO GAINEY, NATHAN 0800 2359\nDUTY DRIVER BRIGMAN, AUSTIN# 0800 2000\nVT-2 Key Contacts:\nSDO Duty Office: (850) 623-7222 / Cell: (850) 450-7508 USN CACO: LT Gainey\nFDO: (850) 623-7350 / 623-7428 / Cell: (850) 393-3199 CMEO: LT Goodpaster\nSAPR 24 Hour Help Line: (877) 995-5247 CMD Financial Specialist:\nVT-2 Ombudsman: (843) 503-8818 CFL: LT McKenzie\nUSMC CACO: Capt Bertella SAPR VA: LT McKenzie / LT Swann / LCDR Cannavo\nUSCG CACO: CDR Hathaway Suicide Assist: Maj Tootill / LT McKenzie"
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "[Sunday]-KNSE CTO 0700-1730 & 2100-2300, KNBJ CLOSED, KNFD CLOSED, K12J CTO ONLY**$, KGZH CTO ONLY**$, KNDZ 1700-2100; CTO 0700-\n1630 & 2100-2300\n*Closes at listed time or sunset, whichever occurs first\n$- RDO and CFR operating hours M-F. Reference R&I 24-07/11 for use w/o RDO or CFR present\n1. Annual Flight Physical and Dental need to be completed by the end of your birth month. Contact Class Advisor for questions.\n2. VR Sims are available to students in building 3125.\n3. Sim standby to check in with sim supervisor and wait in the sim building lounge until end of scheduled standby period.\n4. During weekdays, open OFT or UTD sim lines on the VT-2 flight schedule are available practice sims for VT-2 students. Open sims assigned to VT-\n2 will not be hard scheduled or reserved by any squadron. These are to be utilized on a first come, first serve basis for VT-2 students. Any TW-5\nInstructor Pilot requiring the use of an open sim takes priority.\n5. Marine Student PFT every Wednesday at 0630 USS Intrepid Rd Pull-up bars. Every Thursday Radford Gym NAS Pensacola with MATSG-21. Snivel\nas required.\n6. In-flight photography (PHOTOEX) is authorized on all IP/IP flights to facilitate the positive promotion of Primary Flight Training and the Naval\nAviation Enterprise, not to interfere or supplant scheduled training, and shall be conducted in a safe, professional, and risk adverse manner IAW\nthe requirements set forth in TRAWINGFIVEINST 3710.2 and CNATRAINST 3710.38. Squadron PAO review and CO approval is required prior to\nposting or distributing any in-flight photographs on social media or other mediums of communication.\n7. Students may be scheduled and shall be prepared for 2 flights per day from the FAM4200 block forward, unless specifically prohibited by the\nJPPT. For Cross Country Operations, you may expect to be scheduled for 3 flight/sims per day.\n8. Students SHALL ensure ALL CAIs are completed prior to the execution of simulator or flight events for which they are a prerequisite.\n9. All weekend aircraft MUST be signed for Friday or Saturday. No fuel available after 2000 Saturday at KNSE. No fuel available Sunday at KNSE.\nAircraft issue available Saturday from 0800-1500.\n10. CBRN Mask Fitting \u2013 Required by 25 NOV for all Navy, USMC, USAF SNA and IPs. WALK-INS at BLDG 2994 (next to T-6 Sim Building) Room 2,\n0800-1600 M-F.\nMONTHLY CALENDAR \u2013 SEPTEMBER LONG RANGE CALENDAR\nCBRN MASK FITTING \u2013 ALL NAVY/USMC/USAF \u2013 IP Holiday Party \u2013 05 DEC\n0800-1600 M-F. (Note 10) Holiday Leave Period \u2013 18 DEC-03 JAN\nXMAS 96 \u2013 24-27 DEC\nHicks LFF \u2013 19 NOV New Year 96 \u2013 03 JAN\nMcKenzie LFF \u2013 20 NOV Lake Havasu Detachment \u2013 25 JAN \u2013 05 MAR.\nFriendsgiving (Sikes Hall) \u2013 25 NOV 1100-1400 IP Swap 14 Feb.\nThanksgiving 96 (NO FLY) \u2013 26-29 NOV\nSAFETY DEPARTMENT OPERATIONS OFFICER EXECUTIVE OFFICER COMMANDING OFFICER\nREPRESENTATIVE LCDR J. D. SCARFO CDR L. S. SCHAFF CDR J. L. HATHAWAY"
    },
